Hello Admin Wizards,

Thanks to all who replied, especially to:

Russ Schaefer, Wolfgang Rupp, Kazuro Furukawa, Johan Brusche, Iain 
Barker and Joe Carrico.

Consensus was that if one accepts status "unsupported" it is possible to 
run True64 5.1B-3 on a 8200 with firmware 6.6-15.

As to the assemblance problem, I was pointed to the following documents:
http://www.compaq.com/products/quickspecs/soc_archives/80737.html
http://h18002.www1.hp.com/alphaserver/archive/8400/
http://ftp.digital.com/pub/Digital/Alpha/systems/as8200/docs

What I will probably do is the following:
Since the docs show that it is possible to place a total of 6 disk 
shelves maximum directly into the server rack and since I have just 6 
shelves at all, I will integrate them into the server and stand back 
from reassembling the SW 800 Rack at all - it is too large for the 
elevator anyway and we would have to bring it up to the 4th floor. Quite 
a job!
Will inform the list whether or not it works.
If not, I may have a lot of spare parts for sale ;o)

thanks again
CW

